│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ situated_voice_by_kind                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ **What changed.** The old prompt was one flat list of style rules. This one is a short    │
│                          │ pipeline instead:                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. A tiny reasoning plan with a hard cap on thinking.                                     │
│                          │ 2. A per-kind "situation" card. The model picks one for answer, email, post, note or      │
│                          │ rewrite, and each card sets the register and how the text opens.                          │
│                          │ 3. A general section on texture.                                                          │
│                          │ 4. A final ban list.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Why the restructure.** Every flagged failure used the same textbook shape: define, then │
│                          │ give the mechanism, then the consequence, then a caveat, with tidy causal chaining ("This │
│                          │ is why…"). The only passing text and the target examples look different. They are         │
│                          │ anchored in particulars, move in a lopsided order, and use specific nouns and odd but     │
│                          │ true details. Some are flat and procedural, like a memo or a legal clause.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **How the new prompt uses that.**                                                         │
│                          │ - It makes the model write from inside a concrete situation, not as an explainer.         │
│                          │ - It tells the model to lead with the specific case.                                      │
│                          │ - It aims to break the explanatory cadence: fewer causal connectives, no hedge stacking,  │
│                          │ no three-item lists.                                                                      │
│                          │ - It lets "notes" be clipped, memo-like jottings.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Sampling.** Temperature goes up slightly to 1.0 to raise lexical surprise. Top_p is     │
│                          │ lowered a little to 0.92 so output stays coherent.                                        │
