│                          │ no rhetorical tics. The model obeys them and still writes the same textbook explainer: a  │
│                          │ definition, then support, then a mechanism, in neutral third person. That shape is what   │
│                          │ the detector flags.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The texts the real Pangram passed as human look different. They are first-person and      │
│                          │ opinionated, with hedges like "I guess" and "I mean". They ask rhetorical questions, make │
│                          │ concessions, give a judgement, and use contractions and loose, uneven syntax.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ So this version changes approach. Instead of asking for neutral prose with banned         │
│                          │ patterns, it casts the model as a specific kind of writer: someone replying on a forum or │
│                          │ in an email from their own understanding. That writer:                                    │
│                          │ - uses "I think" and "honestly";                                                          │
│                          │ - answers the asker's actual worry first and skips definitions;                           │
│                          │ - allows asides, small self-corrections and a parenthetical;                              │
│                          │ - ends on an opinion or practical remark rather than a summary.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It sets guardrails to keep the task score high:                                           │
│                          │ - no invented anecdotes, people or numbers (hedged opinion is allowed instead);           │
│                          │ - length targets are kept;                                                                │
│                          │ - rewrites keep every fact but read like the original author venting or recounting.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Reasoning is capped explicitly to avoid empty outputs. Temperature is raised slightly so  │
│                          │ word choice and rhythm vary more.                                                         │
