│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ spoken_voice_persona                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ **What the failures show.** Almost every failure is neutral, explanatory prose. These     │
│                          │ texts open with a topic sentence that restates the question, then give an even chain of   │
│                          │ "X does Y. This is why Z." sentences, then close tidily. The current prompt asks for      │
│                          │ brevity but still produces textbook register. Pangram reads that register as AI no matter │
│                          │ how short it is.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **What the target examples share.** The machine texts that real Pangram passed have       │
│                          │ little in common structurally. They share register instead:                               │
│                          │ - They are first person and opinionated.                                                  │
│                          │ - They react to things ("I guess", "I mean", "Still,").                                   │
│                          │ - They ask the reader or themselves questions.                                            │
│                          │ - They use contractions and parentheticals.                                               │
│                          │ - They read as a little lopsided rather than balanced.                                    │
│                          │ - They take a stance instead of surveying a topic.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **What this candidate does differently.** It is a register-transfer prompt rather than a  │
│                          │ list of banned patterns. The model is told to "say it out loud to someone": first react   │
│                          │ to the question, then talk through the knowledge in a person's spoken-casual voice. It    │
│                          │ includes:                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Concrete voice moves: hedges, side comments in parentheses, one honest question, mild   │
│                          │ opinion, sentences that start with "And" or "But", uneven paragraphing.                   │
│                          │ - An explicit list of textbook signatures to avoid: restating the question, "This is      │
│                          │ why", "The short answer", definition-first openings, balanced survey sentences, and the   │
│                          │ "not X but Y" pattern.                                                                    │
│                          │ - A rule that any personal framing stays vague ("from what I've read", "I've always       │
│                          │ heard") so no facts are invented.                                                         │
│                          │ - Separate handling for emails, posts and rewrites, so tasks stay on target and source    │
│                          │ facts are preserved.                                                                      │
│                          │ - A very short thinking instruction, to avoid empty outputs.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Sampling.** Temperature is raised slightly, to 0.95, for more lexical burstiness while  │
│                          │ staying coherent.                                                                         │
