│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ concrete_case_voice_hotter                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Both earlier prompts produced the same flagged shape. Each output was a tidy explainer    │
│                          │ that opens with a definition ("X is dangerous because...", "The brace position is a..."), │
│                          │ chains causes together with "because/so/which", and gives every point equal space.        │
│                          │ Telling the model to be "casual" only layered "honestly/like" on top of that same         │
│                          │ skeleton, and it still scored 88 to 95.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The texts that passed have a different shape:                                             │
│                          │ - the passing rewrite;                                                                    │
│                          │ - the target examples (reviews, legal text, a regulatory memo).                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ They are anchored in one particular situation. They state concrete things flatly, with    │
│                          │ few explanatory connectives. They carry a slightly uneven, unpolished register and no     │
│                          │ teaching arc.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new prompt makes three changes:                                                       │
│                          │ - It tells the model to anchor on a specific situation or case instead of a definition.   │
│                          │ - It bans the explainer moves: definitional openers, cause chains, "this is why",         │
│                          │ balanced coverage and tidy closers.                                                       │
│                          │ - It allows natural roughness: a fragment, an odd comma, a repeated word, a slightly      │
│                          │ awkward phrasing.                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Fact rules and length rules stay, and the instruction to keep thinking short stays first. │
│                          │ I also raise the temperature modestly to 1.0 to increase lexical unpredictability, which  │
│                          │ detectors key on, without risking incoherence.                                            │
