│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ casual_redditor_highertemp                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Both earlier prompts got the model to drop the obvious AI tics, but the outputs still     │
│                          │ read as textbook exposition. Most of them open by defining or restating the topic ("X is  │
│                          │ dangerous because...", "In an aircraft emergency, the brace position is...") and then run │
│                          │ evenly through a mechanism: "because" leads to "so", one point per sentence. Pangram keys │
│                          │ on that cadence.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The human-labeled targets look different. They read like reviews and messages, with a     │
│                          │ situational, opinionated, uneven texture. The one passing output was a rewrite full of    │
│                          │ grounded specifics and some irritation.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit makes three changes:                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - **Commenter voice.** The model now writes as a commenter reacting to the question       │
│                          │ rather than an explainer.                                                                 │
│                          │ - **Banned textbook moves.** It explicitly bans the moves seen in the failures: a         │
│                          │ definitional opener, restating the question, step-by-step causal chains, and evenly       │
│                          │ weighted coverage. It asks instead for one main point, some imperfect connective tissue   │
│                          │ and mild opinion.                                                                         │
│                          │ - **Higher temperature.** It raises temperature to 1.05 to increase token-level           │
│                          │ unpredictability. That is moderate enough for a 27B model to stay coherent.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Reasoning stays short to avoid empty outputs. The fact-invention rules and length/rewrite │
│                          │ rules are kept to protect the task score.                                                 │
