│ patch_description        │ Both earlier prompts still produced explainer prose. That covers the casual-voice version │
│                          │ and the terse-expert version. The texts read as tidy, complete, mechanism-by-mechanism    │
│                          │ explanations, and Pangram flagged nearly all of them.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The texts that pass, both the passing rewrite and the target examples, share a few        │
│                          │ traits:                                                                                   │
│                          │ - They are grounded in concrete situations.                                               │
│                          │ - They read like someone recounting or reacting, not teaching.                            │
│                          │ - They use plain declarative sentences with slightly clumsy word choice.                  │
│                          │ - Their coverage is uneven and incomplete.                                                │
│                          │ - They have mild roughness, such as repeated words ("I guess... I guess") and imperfect   │
│                          │ punctuation.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new prompt makes that the core persona: a non-writer typing a comment or email. It    │
│                          │ gives these instructions:                                                                 │
│                          │ - Anchor the answer in a concrete everyday example rather than an abstract definition.    │
│                          │ - Skip textbook framing ("X is a...", "The short answer is", "mainly because", "This is   │
│                          │ why").                                                                                    │
│                          │ - Allow light imperfections like repeated words and loose punctuation.                    │
│                          │ - Keep only one or two points.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It also bans the specific stock openings seen in the failures. It keeps the reasoning     │
│                          │ budget instruction short and preserves the rules on accuracy, length and rewrites.        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The temperature is raised moderately to 1.05. This flattens token predictability, which   │
│                          │ detectors key on. Task scores (around 8) leave some margin to absorb the change.          │
